Built bottom-up: leaf numeric/string helpers → row transforms → whole-file writes (byte-identical IDAT and every ancillary chunk) → whole-file reads with every transform → progressive reader, [38;5;10mpng_read_png[0m/[38;5;10mpng_write_png[0m, simplified API → malformed input and error strings → remaining struct-based entry points → callbacks and file APIs → randomized fuzzing. A 60× fuzz sweep ([38;5;10mPNG_FUZZ_SCALE=60[0m, ~75 s) covering ~36 000 random encode/decode pairs, ~90 000 mutated-file decodes and progressive-reader fuzzing is also clean.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Three divergences turned out to be C undefined behaviour rather than translation defects, and the tests avoid them deliberately (documented inline): [38;5;10mpng_handle_tRNS[0m copies uninitialized stack bytes into [38;5;10minfo_ptr->trans_alpha[0m for non-palette images; [38;5;10mpng_read_png[0m leaves the padding bits past the image width in its [38;5;10mpng_malloc[0m'd rows indeterminate; and [38;5;10mpng_convert_to_rfc1123_buffer[0m dereferences a NULL [38;5;10mpng_time[0m. One other early failure was my own test error — an out-of-range [38;5;10mbackground.blue[0m of 300 made C index past its 256-entry gamma table.[0m[0m
